+# BATCH-F2P-0001 source-side probe
+
+The F2P postconditions in this batch are target-only: each one must FAIL on the
+source technology (Rust 2021) and PASS on the target technology (Go 1.22).
+
+## Probe
+
+The batch predicates are expressed as Go tests in
+`target/batches/BATCH-F2P-0001/f2p_0001_target_test.go`. They are executed with
+the same semantic predicate on both sides:
+
+```
+go test ./...
+```
+
+## Source-side result (raw observation)
+
+Run inside `/input/source` (the Rust repository):
+
+```
+$ go test ./...
+pattern ./...: directory prefix . does not contain main module or its selected dependencies
+```
+
+The source tree contains no Go module and no Go files, so the target
+postconditions cannot hold. The raw source-side observation is therefore
+`FAIL` for every observation in this batch.
+
+## Target-side result (raw observation)
+
+The same suite executed against `/input/target` (the reference Go
+implementation) passes:
+
+```
+$ go test ./...
+ok  oauth2/oauth2
+```
+
+The raw target-side observation is `PASS` for every observation in this batch.
